From: Aqueous maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] scene: skip transforming empty buffer damage

Keep buffer ownership, cached texture invalidation, wait timeline updates and
mapping/size damage intact. Once those updates are complete, an explicitly
empty damage region cannot affect any output. Avoid coordinate lookup, region
transforms, scaling and output traversal in this common commit path. A NULL
damage region still means full damage.

--- a/types/scene/wlr_scene.c
+++ b/types/scene/wlr_scene.c
@@ -1040,6 +1040,13 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	// Buffer ownership, texture invalidation, synchronization and geometry
+	// updates above still apply even when the client supplied no damage.
+	// Transforming an empty region cannot damage any output.
+	if (options->damage != NULL && pixman_region32_empty(options->damage)) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	int lx, ly;
 	if (!wlr_scene_node_coords(&scene_buffer->node, &lx, &ly)) {
 		return;
